     4	/**
     5	 * The items one issued policy covers: what they are insured for all together,
     6	 * and which of them a reported damage was suffered by.
     7	 *
     8	 * Two decisions live here, and the MHPCO makes them for separate reasons. The
     9	 * matching rule says which covered item answers to a reported damage -- by
    10	 * type today, by an item the damage names outright tomorrow, and one insured
    11	 * item per reported damage once the office starts counting them. The refusal
    12	 * rule says what the office does when a damage names something this policy
    13	 * does not cover: it declines the whole claim rather than settling the rest of
    14	 * the incident around it.
    15	 *
    16	 * Not to be confused with {@link InsurableItems}, which decides what the
    17	 * office will take on at all; this says what one issued policy already covers.
    18	 */
    19	public final class CoveredItems implements Coverage {
    20	
    21	    private final List<Item> insuredItems;
    22	
    23	    public CoveredItems(List<Item> insuredItems) {
    24	        this.insuredItems = List.copyOf(insuredItems);
    25	    }
    26	
    27	    /**
    28	     * What these items are insured for, all together: each at its own
    29	     * insurance value, summed. What the MHPCO charged to insure them does not
    30	     * enter into it -- neither a risk surcharge nor the component block offer
    31	     * moves the insurance sum.
    32	     */
    33	    public int insuranceSum() {
    34	        return insuredItems.stream()
    35	                .mapToInt(InsuranceValues::insuranceValueOf)
    36	                .sum();
    37	    }
    38	
    39	    /**
    40	     * The insured item the reported damage was suffered by, or the office's
    41	     * refusal of the whole claim when this policy covers no such item.
    42	     */
    43	    @Override
    44	    public Item damagedIn(Damage damage) {
    45	        return matching(damage).orElseThrow(() -> notCovered(damage));
    46	    }
    47	
    48	    /**
    49	     * Which covered item answers to a reported damage: the first one of the
    50	     * damaged type.
    51	     */
    52	    private Optional<Item> matching(Damage damage) {
    53	        return insuredItems.stream()
    54	                .filter(item -> item.type().equals(damage.itemType()))
    55	                .findFirst();
    56	    }
    57	
    58	    /**
    59	     * The office declines a damage it covers no item for.
    60	     */
    61	    private static IllegalArgumentException notCovered(Damage damage) {
    62	        return new IllegalArgumentException(
    63	                "This policy does not cover an item of type " + damage.itemType());
    64	    }
